# Day 44 – Teleoperation Refinement

**Date:** 10 August 2026

---

## Objective

Improve MIGRO's keyboard teleoperation system by introducing continuous velocity publishing and a safety timeout.

---

## Work Completed

### 1. Reviewed the Existing Teleoperation System

The Day 43 implementation successfully established manual keyboard control using ROS 2 and `TwistStamped`.

Today's objective was to make the system safer and more representative of a real robot teleoperation interface.

### 2. Implemented Continuous Velocity Publishing

The teleoperation node was modified to maintain the desired velocity and publish commands continuously using a ROS 2 timer.

The node now publishes velocity commands at a regular interval instead of relying on a single command being sent for each keypress.

### 3. Implemented Keyboard Timeout Safety

A keyboard input timeout was introduced.

If no keyboard input is received for a defined period, the node automatically publishes zero velocity.

This provides a basic fail-safe mechanism:

```text
Operator input
      ↓
Velocity command
      ↓
MIGRO moves

Input stops
      ↓
Timeout
      ↓
Zero velocity
      ↓
MIGRO stops